    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360-a1">

                <pb facs="0641" n="507" xml:id="pg507"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 292.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commercial Agency of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Noumea</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-12-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 8, 1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch of the 17th September last,
                    containing inclosure on convict question is at hand.</p>
                <p>By this occasion I inclose extracts from the official journal, one referring to
                    mail service between Tahiti and San Francisco; the other, informing convicts of
                    the fourth category, first section, that they will no longer receive permission
                    to land in the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William E.
                    Morgan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
